  "current_behavior": "On e2def07 the catalog manifest lists only fixture.example plus identity.toml. No control.vulnerability.* / evidence.vulnerability.* exist. ISO pack keeps hybrid vulnerability.remediation. weeping-angel-assurance::bridge emits security_finding observations (canonical_type security.vulnerability.present / secret.exposure / dependency_confusion_risk) without status, owner, SLA clock, or coverage completeness. Prompt 03 can evaluate NoneSubjects but the SLA handoff example is not wired to findings. Empty scans are already documented as not Effective, but no catalog test encodes that.",
  "desired_behavior": "Add a 20-control vulnerability family (15–25 band) under catalog/canonical/v1 with evidence.vulnerability|secret|dependency|*software-inventory facts and population tests (scan current/coverage, no critical/high over SLA, owners, no active secrets, exception expiry, FP vs resolved). Ten golden fixtures distinguish clean, inside-SLA, overdue, approved/expired exception, 8/10 coverage, stale scan, active secret, duplicates, and zero-findings-unknown-coverage. Consume CanonicalCatalog, EvidenceValue, and Prompt 03 arms. Do not rewrite ISO pack, IAM catalog, or scanner engines. A finding is never a compliance result.",
